I like the idea of Tashlan as a neutral deity -- it definitely rides
the fence. As you say though, one of the big issues is that there *is*
no Tashlan.

It's just hard to shoehorn Monotheism into a Polytheistic setting. :)

Just as Tash is one of the lesser (but very real) beings in Narnia,
perhaps we could take one of the other lesser (but somewhat above
human) beings. The two major ones that I'm thinking of are Father Time
and Bacchus. Both have their advantages as deities -- Father Time is
more impartial through asceticism, but Bacchus is impartial through
apathy and hedonism. Either one could really work though.

